Z||000000||fierospeeder||12-12-2000||04:49 AM||||Got the news today, just going nuts.  Dont know if its really going to happen or not.<P>Heres the story, <P>my girlfriend has a daughter that is 2 years old with her exboyfriend that lives in detroit.  Currently my girlfriend lives with her sister about 4 miles away from me, and we see each other about everyday.<P>Her exboyfriend, isn't the greatest guy around, he has been physically violent to her, and is very controlling.  Last time she was with him, he grabbed her neck and she left the same day.  She has given him about 4 chances and they never worked.  I do have letters that she wrote on her own realizing that he is a bastard, etc...<P>Her daughter is staying at her dads for 2-3 weeks just for a visit.  And today my girlfriend tells me she is going to move there.  Because she wants her daughter to have a complete family.  I told her, this will make her worse,daughter, as when she grows up, he will show signs of a bad father, and as a abusive person to her mom.  When she was pregnant, he cheated on her with a 16 year old, and got her pregnant.  He was 25.  later he was arrested for harboring a teen.  He also paid for her abortion.  greatest dad figure?<P>I asked her why, this was on the phone, and we had the foot of snow so going to her house wasn't really possible, i will this morning.  <P>She said the above, her daughter having two parents.  And she said he has counseling and he is better now.   Im pretty sure she said that before and it didn't work out.  "Cant teach a new "dog" new tricks"   <P>I hate it that she has a kid with him, and how he blackmales her with her kid, which i think is happening.  Because he wants her to live there.  I should get her pregnant but my mom would kick my ass so i can do the same bullE***$<P>I helped her so much, and she is having a better life now living here with me, and her daughter would be better off here with me or atleast this evironment.  Detroit is so low down, ive been there.  <P>I dont want to lose her, and i know people asked relationship advice in here before.  Shes going to waste her life, and i dont want to see that happen, and i think she plans on living there forever.<P>I know it wont last, because the other 4 times she gave him chances.   Her sister just got a new job at a hospital and she can get my g/f if she still is a job, and also a 35,000 dollar tuition for college, which she never finished because of this bastard getting her pregnant.<P>thanks u guys<BR>i always have u guys and my cars<BR>  ||||reg||1
Z||000001||mbramble||12-12-2000||07:25 AM||||First and foremost -- don't get her pregnant!!  Secondly, she needs counselling as much as her abusive boyfriend does.  Any woman who willingly continues to go back into that situation has problems of her own.  Personally, I'd say it's time to cut loose from that relationship; you're the one who's gonna lose out in all this mess.<P>Mike<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000002||GT Bastard||12-12-2000||08:01 AM||||I agree that the best thing to do is to let her go, but I know I wouldn't be able to do that if it was somebody I truely cared for.  Maybe try contacting some sort of battered-womans counseler.  I'm sure they'd have better luck trying to talk some sense into her. It's better that she do everything in her power to keep this psycho dad away from her kids through legal action.  And really, it's her only chance at giving the kid a healthy childhood.  Otherwise, she's going to have a terribly unhappy life and kid is likely going to become his dad.  Believe me, this world has enough assholes as it is... I think it's pretty obvious which situation would be better for everyone.  Does her family know about this?  If not, make them aware!  And DON'T GET HER PREGNANT!!!||||reg||1
Z||000003||Julian||12-12-2000||10:47 AM||||100% agree with the previous 2 posts....DON'T KNOCK HER UP! <P>Your best move is to move on... let her be... get into another relationship or she will always use you to fall back on. Tell her you are SERIOUSLY getting into another relationship and bid her farewell. I'm sure she's great but do you want to deal with her ex & her kid for the rest of your life.... WAKE UP BOY, you drive a Fiero you can have any woman you want!<P>Seriously....try & move on.||||reg||13
Z||000004||JohnnyK||12-12-2000||12:02 PM||||Agreed... You'd have to put up with him for the rest of your life.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Songman||12-12-2000||12:15 PM||||Yeah, it makes you mad when you hear about stories like this... She deserves better, you deserve better, and without a doubt the child deserves better!<P>But... as silly as we all know it is, it is still her choice. When (if) she finally realizes what she is putting herself and her child through and takes active steps to stop it, she may finally have a life. But my family has always told me something that I didn't realize until I was 35 years old and looking back at bad relationships. You try to help people. That is a good human quality. But, only to a point. It is much easier for someone to drag you down with them than it is for you to bring them up.<P>I know you love her. And I know it hurts. You have given her every chance you could but she still chose to go back into a life she knows is hell. Make her live with that choice. Do not be there when she comes crying back, becase she will! And then she will leave again and come back.. See the pattern? I've been there! Be a man and stand your ground.<P>There are women out there who would love to have the situation that you tried to give her. Give some of them a chance. You didn't say how old you are but I assume you are fairly young. Enjoy your life. You have a lot yet to come. Be ready for it!||||reg||8
Z||000006||DJRice||12-12-2000||02:57 PM||||You should definitely not get her pregnant.  This guy will <B><I>always</B></I> be a part of her life, and the child will always be a bond between them.  Nothing you can do will ever change that.  If she thinks that she wants to go back to him, not much good can come from you trying to fight it.  She obviously has made up her mind (even though it sounds like she is out of her mind) and once the mind is made up you might as well talk to a wall.  <BR>Some women seem to stick to those who abuse them because they think that things will change.  9 times out of 10 they wont change.  <P>It may hurt for a while, Its probably best for you to let her go.  ||||reg||1
